T}
T{
flac
T}@T{
flac
T}
T{
pcm_*
T}@T{
the same PCM codec
T}
.TE
.PP
An input with any other audio codec is rejected before any work starts.
There is no automatic conversion to another codec.
.SH OUTPUT FILES
The input and output extensions must match, and input and output must be
different files.
.PP
The output is written to a temporary file in the same directory and
renamed over \f[I]watermarked_video\f[R] only after it is complete.
If processing fails, an existing output file is left unchanged.
.SH TOOLS
\f[B]videowmark\f[R] looks for \f[B]ffmpeg\f[R], \f[B]ffprobe\f[R] and
\f[B]audiowmark\f[R] beside its own executable first, then on the search
path.
In the bundled release packages the sibling programs are required, and
the search path is not used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
The operation completed successfully.
.TP
\f[B]>0\f[R]
An error occurred.
Messages are printed to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the legacy codec and bit rate summary for a file:
.PP
\f[CR]videowmark probe input.mp4\f[R]
.PP
Embed a 32\-digit hexadecimal message into a video:
.PP
\f[CR]videowmark add input.mp4 output.mp4 0123456789abcdef0011223344556677\f[R]
.PP
Retrieve the message from a watermarked video:
.PP
\f[CR]videowmark get output.mp4\f[R]
